---
layout: base.njk
pageScripts: [country-map.js]
pagination:
  data: db.countries
  size: 1
  alias: c
permalink: "/countries/{{ c.iso2Lower }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ c.name }}"
  description: "Climate regions, major cities and seed sources in {{ c.name }}."
  jsonUrl: "/countries/{{ c.iso2Lower }}.json"
---
{% set crumbs = [{href: "/countries/", label: "Countries"}, {label: c.name, current: true}] %}{% include "crumbs.njk" %}
<article data-pagefind-body>
  <h1>{% set cc = c.iso2 %}{% include "flag.njk" %} {{ c.name }}</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    {% if c.capital %}Capital: {% if c.capitalPlace %}<a href="{{ c.capitalPlace.placeUrl | url }}">{{ c.capital }}</a>{% else %}{{ c.capital }}{% endif %}.{% endif %}
    ISO 3166-1 alpha-2: {{ c.iso2 }}.
  </p>

  {% if c.mapView or c.mapBounds %}
    {% set mapView = c.mapView %}
    {% set mapBounds = c.mapBounds %}
    {% set outline = c.outline %}
    {% set svgPath = c.svgPath %}
    {% set pin = null %}
    {% set legendRegions = c.regionShares %}
    {% set mapLabel = "Köppen–Geiger climate map of " + c.name %}
    {% set caption %}Köppen–Geiger climate map (Beck et al. 2018, CC BY 4.0) with a simplified country outline from Natural Earth Admin 0 1:50m (public domain). The view is fitted to the principal land cluster and may omit far-flung territories. The inset without JavaScript is a static SVG of the same view.{% endset %}
    {% include "climate-map.njk" %}
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Climate regions</h2>
  {% if c.regionShares.length %}
    {% if c.climateMethod == "area" %}
    <p>Approximate share of this country’s land, from 0.5° grid cells assigned with Natural Earth 50m boundaries. Shares under 0.1% are omitted. Overseas holdings in the same country record are included in the percentages even if they fall outside the inset map.</p>
    {% elif c.climateMethod == "cities" %}
    <p>This territory is too small (or is missing from the 50m boundaries) for a reliable 0.5° area share. The figures below are the climate at a sample of {{ c.climate.sample_count }} GeoNames capital or city point{{ 's' if c.climate.sample_count != 1 else '' }}, not an area percentage.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <table class="zones-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Climate region</th><th>{% if c.climateMethod == "cities" %}Share of sampled points{% else %}Approx. land share{% endif %}</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for r in c.regionShares %}
        <tr>
          <th><a href="{{ r.url | url }}"><span class="swatch sm" style="background:{{ r.color }}"></span> {{ r.name }}</a></th>
          <td>{{ r.share }}%</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {% if c.koppen.length %}
    <p>Köppen–Geiger classes:
      {% for k in c.koppen %}{{ k.code | kgLink(koppen.classes, db.kgToRegion, true) | safe }} {{ k.share }}%{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  {% else %}
    <p>No climate share is listed at 0.5° resolution: this territory has no Beck grid cell centre inside a Natural Earth 50m boundary, and no GeoNames capital or city sample landed on a classified land cell. That is a data gap, not a claim that it has no climate.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% set growsWell = c.growsWell %}
  {% set placeName = c.name %}
  {% set intro = "These crops have a sourced growing guide for a climate region listed for " + c.name + ". This is not a list of traditional or typical crops. Country-level hardiness zones are not in the dataset, so this list does not filter by zone. Crops with a recorded hardiness range still show that range on the card." %}
  {% include "grows-well.njk" %}

  <h2>Major cities</h2>
  {% if c.cities.length %}
  <ul class="city-list">
    {% for city in c.cities %}
    <li><a href="{{ city.placeUrl | url }}">{{ city.name }}</a>{% if city.adminName %}<span class="muted">, {{ city.adminName }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="small muted">Cities are the most populous GeoNames <code>cities15000</code> places in {{ c.name }} (CC BY 4.0). Links go to a city page at <code>/places/&lt;slug&gt;/</code> when one exists; the same slug also works as <code>?place=</code> on the home map.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p>No city from the GeoNames <code>cities15000</code> gazetteer is listed for this territory.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Seed sources</h2>
  {% if c.seedSources.length %}
  <ul>
    {% for s in c.seedSources %}
    <li><a href="{{ s.url }}">{{ s.name }}</a>{% if s.kind %} <span class="muted">({{ s.kind }})</span>{% endif %}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% else %}
  <p>No seed source in the catalogue is listed for {{ c.name }} yet.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="small muted">{{ db.climateAttribution }} {% if db.outlineAttribution %}{{ db.outlineAttribution }} {% endif %}Names from GeoNames (CC BY 4.0).</p>
  <p class="meta">{% set jsonHref = "/countries/" + c.iso2Lower + ".json" %}{% include "raw-data.njk" %}</p>
</article>
